index 0000000..636b8fa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/legacy-origin/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Old-origin deployment (`https://app.dailygrind.example.com`)
+
+These files hand the installed app over to `https://dailygrind.example.com`.
+Both hosts share the registrable domain `example.com`, which Web App Origin
+Migration requires (same-site only).
+
+1. **Authorize the move (required).** Serve
+   `.well-known/web-app-origin-association` at
+   `https://app.dailygrind.example.com/.well-known/web-app-origin-association`
+   with `Content-Type: application/json`. Without this file the browser ignores
+   the new site's `migrate_from` claim.
+2. **Prompt existing users early (optional).** Merge the `migrate_to` key from
+   `manifest-migrate-to.json` into the old site's existing manifest, so
+   installed users get migrated without having to visit the new site first.
+3. **Fallback banner.** Paste `migration-banner.html` into the old site's pages
+   for browsers that don't support migration (Firefox, Safari, Chromium < 149).
+
+The new origin's side lives in `/manifest.webmanifest` (`migrate_from`).
+To make the move mandatory, change `"behavior": "suggest"` to `"force"` there.
+The browser then asks the user to **Update** or **Remove**; it never removes
+the old app silently.
+
+What migration does **not** carry over: localStorage, IndexedDB, cookies and
+permissions (notifications, location) stay with the old origin. Move any
+per-user data through the account backend or cross-origin messaging.
